    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="0854" n="842" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg842"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Chile/471b: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-01T19:15:00-04:00">June 1, 1943—7:15
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–862. With respect to the control of exports of refined and semimanufactured
                    copper from Chile, the Department desires to bring to the Embassy’s attention a
                    paragraph in despatch no. 327 of May 17, 1943, from Buenos Aires,<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d807-f1"/> reading as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p><hi rendition="#italic">“Copper and Copper products</hi>—Heavy imports of
                            copper and copper products from Chile continue despite the fact that
                            stocks in the Argentine are believed to approach minimum requirements
                            for the rest of 1943. An appreciable portion of these stocks are held by
                            the black-listed firm Sema,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d807-f2"/> which firm
                            has succeeded in augmenting its stocks during recent months. Copper is
                            rapidly becoming an allservice metal in the Argentine economy, replacing
                            for many uses other <pb facs="0855" n="843" xml:id="pg843"/> metals. So
                            abundant are supplies that manufacturers who formerly only worked with
                            used bronze or copper now purchase the new product.[”]</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
